  "notes": "w64devkit fortran ZIP: portable MinGW-w64 GCC 13.1.0 with gfortran, gcc, g++, binutils, GDB and GNU Make. Use it to compile .f/.f90 files, create native Windows executables, run Makefile builds and debug with gdb from OpenMind terminals. Only these toolchain commands are added to OpenMind terminals (as small launchers); the other programs w64devkit ships (find, sort, tar, bash ...) are not, so Windows' own commands keep working. Its gcc/g++ also build C and C++ when the LLVM-MinGW toolchain isn't installed; Run Code labels them as coming from this runtime. The system PATH is not changed.",
